      "caption": "AAV9-GBA1 ICV delivery into mice produces robust expression of active hGCase in the brain (A) Vector genome biodistribution, as measured by genomic copies (GC)/\u03bcg DNA, was quantified in the cortex (left) and striatum (right) from D409V+/+ mice injected with 1 \u00d7 109 (pink, n = 9), 7 \u00d7 109 (green, n = 13), 1 \u00d7 1010 (purple, n = 10), and 4 \u00d7 1010 (light blue, n = 23) total GC of AAV9-GBA1. (B) Representative images of in situ hybridization staining for hGBA1 mRNA from coronal mouse brain sections. From left to right, images of WT control mice (injected with AAV9-YFP at 4 \u00d7 1010 GC) and D409V+/+ mice injected with 1 \u00d7 109, 7 \u00d7 109, 1 \u00d7 1010, and 4 \u00d7 1010 total GC doses. (C) GCase activity (nmol/mg/h) in the cortex (left) and striatum (right) from WT mice injected with AAV9-YFP 4 \u00d7 1010 GC dose (WT control, gray; n = 21) and D409V+/+ mice injected with a range of doses: AAV9-YFP 4 \u00d7 1010 GC dose (\u201cControl,\u201d black; n = 22) and AAV9-GBA1 1 \u00d7 109 (pink, n = 18), 7 \u00d7 109 (green, n = 23), 1 \u00d7 1010 (purple, n = 20), and 4 \u00d7 1010 (light blue, n = 33 cortex and n = 31 striatum) total GC. Scale bar represents 1 mm. Mixed-effects model with Dunnett\u2019s multiple comparisons test. Data are presented as medians and min to max. **p < 0.01, ***p < 0.001, and ****p < 0.0001. www.moleculartherapy.org Molecular Therapy: Advances Vol. 34 September 2026 3",
